+### L-seasonal-flora-3748 — Folded plant lighting and the four seasonal viewing choices
+**Liberty:** prairie leaf and grass normals follow the existing folds, species scales, arch and wind. These normals suggest fine curvature without adding geometry or altering the plant's deterministic placement, outline or wind. Crop leaves use the shared artistic thin-leaf light, shadowed with the sun, and capable devices reuse their existing colour atlas for slight relief; weak devices and Light omit that relief sampling. Native wall ivy derives a leaf mask from its original green atlas and vertex colours before seasonal or evidence recolouring, keeping brown stems out of the leaf-light term. These are render approximations, not measured species scattering. Light uses a cheaper environment response on eligible nonmetal standard materials (base roughness at least 0.65): the existing sky-and-ground diffuse convolution supplies the environment, with a fixed 0.04 dielectric share and 0.96 diffuse share; direct highlights use single-scatter GGX. Thin-leaf transmission, directional and point shadows, wind, maps, instancing and density remain. Full and Balanced compile the original physical lighting unchanged. This Light approximation does not identify historical plant optics or claim hardware FPS. Mid-April withholds the July flora's flower heads and their peduncles; it does not introduce an invented spring species roster. Existing crop phenology is retained. The legacy deciduous thicket and vine leaf cards are withheld in winter in the colour and both shadow passes, retaining their woody tubes; evergreen crowns use the separate grown path. All four scene years offer the same seasonal viewing choice. The scene's own calendar season retains its target date (1871 remains 8 October); choosing summer in an autumn-dated scene uses 15 July. Dated jaunts still take their own documented dates and restore the visitor's choice. Scale/needle leaf tiles retain their own evergreen colour through winter; no new historical evergreen planting is inferred.
+**Evidence:** existing species, flower and crop records remain the authority for what is planted. The other-season appearances are viewing approximations under L-season-view-2481, not records of Chicago on those dates. No new asset, density, historical source or species occurrence is introduced.
+**How to resolve:** observed phenology by species and date, calibrated normals and measured leaf optics could replace these broad seasonal and shading approximations.
+**Ticket:** T-3748.
+**Recorded:** 2026-11-25 (T-3748).
+
+### L-1871-grown-context-3760 — A generic grown deciduous proxy for the pre-fire context planting
+**Liberty:** the 1871 context's existing sparse reconstructed planting now draws through the shared adaptive seasonal tree renderer instead of its portable kit's rounded solid crowns. The proxy uses the grown open deciduous habit also used by the street elms, bounded by each context record's nominal height and crown width. It does not identify any context tree as an elm. Its positions, reconstructed grades, source limits and inspection identities remain those of L-1871-city-baseline. Spring, summer and fall use that renderer's corresponding leaf cover, and winter uses bare wood. The shared Trees setting and confidence hide apply to the handed-off records. No context planting is moved or removed by this renderer change.
+**Evidence:** upstream 172bbb62b9ff07352a683a291bf34ea6d392b57d contains 3,543 context and 6,693 street trees. A refreshed audit of all 10,236 trunk centres finds none strictly more than 0.25 m inside 38,598 context building plans or 19 named solid footprint parts. No cross-set trunk centres are closer than two metres. The old pumping-works record is absent upstream. Earlier prototype placement deletions are superseded, and no current planting is withdrawn. These narrow tests do not prove crown clearance or establish that an individual historical tree occupied a reconstructed position. The upstream fire's bare/charred state is retained across seasonal and detail rebuilds.
+**How to resolve:** period views or parcel planting evidence can replace a generic record with a sourced location and habit. Preserve the generic reconstruction label until that evidence exists.
+**Ticket:** T-3760.
+**Recorded:** 2026-11-25 (T-3760).
